# EKPI environment placeholders.
#
# The current code reads:
#   EKP_GOVERNANCE_DATA  - local governance ledger path
#   EKPI_LOCAL_AUTH_USER, EKPI_LOCAL_AUTH_PASSWORD, EKPI_LOCAL_AUTH_ROLE
#                        - one local workbench account (no default account)
#   EKPI_COOKIE_SECURE   - set to 1 to add Secure to the session cookie
# The application does not load a .env file automatically.
# Copy this file to a local, git-ignored location only if you set variables in your shell.

# Local governance web prototype (loopback only):
# EKP_GOVERNANCE_DATA=%LOCALAPPDATA%\EKPI\governance-ledger.jsonl

# Local workbench login. Choose a long password; never commit a real value.
# Without both user and password the server starts but data pages return 401.
# EKPI_LOCAL_AUTH_USER=operator
# EKPI_LOCAL_AUTH_PASSWORD=
# EKPI_LOCAL_AUTH_ROLE=editor
# EKPI_COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Do not put real secrets in this example or in version control.
# If a future feature needs credentials, add a code reference, a test and documentation first.
